  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine is linked to Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through a series of indications that suggest a potential therapeutic relationship. The evidence indicates that Tretamine is associated with Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn is linked to Belotecan and Hydroxyurea, both of which are indicated for Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma. This suggests a possible pathway where Tretamine may influence the development or progression of ovarian small cell carcinoma, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The overlapping indications between Tretamine and other drugs targeting similar tumors imply a potential role in the treatment or prevention of this malignancy. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further research is needed to clarify how Tretamine interacts with these pathways.",
